@region header
GHSS auction 19-20 September 2026 · Scott 90 · E grill

@region title
# Scott 90 — 1868 12¢ black Washington, E grill

National Bank Note Company · line-engraved intaglio · perf. 12 · issued third week of February 1868 (~1,000,000). Charles Steel’s E grill — 11 × 13 mm, points down — broke the fibers so cancel ink could not be washed. From 1 January 1868 this denomination paid the new 12¢ half-ounce treaty rate to Great Britain (down from 24¢; it would fall to 6¢ in 1870). Packets out of New York for Liverpool. Scott U.S. Specialized 2023 used $400; condition as you see. Notes after [The Swedish Tiger](https://www.theswedishtiger.com/90-scotts.html).

@narrative
  - en-US: |
      Ladies and gentlemen — Scott ninety.
      [pause]
      The eighteen sixty-eight twelve-cent black Washington. National Bank Note Company. Line-engraved. Perforated twelve.
      [pause]
      Issued the third week of February, eighteen sixty-eight — about a million printed. Three years after Appomattox, the Post Office was still fighting a very practical fraud: washed stamps used a second time. Charles Steel’s grill is the answer — eleven by thirteen millimetres, points down, an E grill. The paper is bruised so the cancel soaks in.
  - en-US: |
      Look at Washington in the oval. That is National Bank Note lathework — a portrait built for a treaty.
      [pause]
      On the first of January, eighteen sixty-eight, the letter rate to Great Britain was cut from twenty-four cents to twelve cents the half-ounce. This stamp is that rate. New York to Liverpool — Cunard, Inman, the American packets. With a three-cent companion it also made France. Off cover it is still a make-up for heavy domestic mail.
  - en-US: |
      Scott United States Specialized, twenty twenty-three: used, four hundred dollars. This example has the usual classic wear — creases, a small top-margin split, short perfs — inspect it on the millimetre grid and then decide.
      [pause]
      Measure the E lattice against B through J and Z. Then bid — this is Scott ninety.

