@region header
GHSS auction 19-20 September 2026 · Scott 91 · E grill

@region title
# Scott 91 — 1868 15¢ black Lincoln, E grill

National Bank Note Company · plate 41 · ~500,000 · same E grill as Scott 90. The vignette is H. B. Hall’s Sons’ memorial bust — America’s first mourning stamp, issued after Lincoln’s assassination and then grilled for 1868. Fifteen cents paid the 1857 treaty rate to France (per ¼ oz, American or British packet) and the registered-mail fee; also seen to Belgium, Germany, and Switzerland. Scott U.S. Specialized 2023 used $575. Notes after [The Swedish Tiger](https://www.theswedishtiger.com/91-scotts.html).

@narrative
  - en-US: |
      Scott ninety-one.
      [pause]
      Fifteen-cent black Lincoln. National Bank Note. Plate forty-one. About half a million with the E grill.
      [pause]
      The face is older than the grill. Eighteen sixty-six — the first United States mourning stamp. H. B. Hall’s Sons engraved the bust after the assassination. Grilling it in eighteen sixty-eight put that memorial portrait onto registered letters and onto the Atlantic.
  - en-US: |
      Fifteen cents was a European rate. Under the eighteen fifty-seven treaty with France, a quarter-ounce letter was fifteen cents — American packet direct, or via England. The same stamp paid Belgium and the German states, and it paid the registered-mail fee once that fee came down to fifteen cents.
      [pause]
      Look at the eyes in the detailed view. That is the portrait that went to Paris, to Aachen, to London with a New York Paid All marking.
  - en-US: |
      Same E grill as the twelve-cent — eleven by thirteen millimetres. Compare the lattice. Perfs a little irregular, as grilled classics often are.
      [pause]
      Scott United States Specialized, twenty twenty-three: used, five hundred seventy-five dollars. Then bid — this is Scott ninety-one.

