@region header
GHSS auction 19-20 September 2026 · Scott 98 · F grill

@region title
# Scott 98 — 1868 15¢ black Lincoln, F grill

Same National Bank Note Lincoln as Scott 91; the catalog change is the grill. F is the production grill that followed E: about 9 × 13 mm, 11–12 × 15–17 points, points down — narrower, easier to separate than the experimental letters. Same 15¢ work: France, the North German Union, registered mail with a 3¢ companion for domestic postage. Scott U.S. Specialized 2023 used $275. Notes after [The Swedish Tiger](https://www.theswedishtiger.com/98-scotts.html).

@narrative
  - en-US: |
      Scott ninety-eight.
      [pause]
      Still the fifteen-cent Lincoln — now with the F grill.
      [pause]
      Same die, same mourning portrait. The Post Office had learned that A, B, C, and D were too large to tear cleanly. E worked. F is smaller still — about nine by thirteen millimetres — the grill you meet most often on this design.
  - en-US: |
      The rates do not change with the letter. Fifteen cents to France by packet. Fifteen cents as a registry fee, usually with a three-cent stamp paying the domestic letter. Covers to the German states via Aachen Franco.
      [pause]
      If you are choosing between ninety-one and ninety-eight, you are choosing a lattice, not a president. Measure F against E on the overlay.
  - en-US: |
      A strong impression on this example, and a grill you can read. Scott United States Specialized, twenty twenty-three: used, two hundred seventy-five dollars.
      [pause]
      Then bid — this is Scott ninety-eight.

