@region header
GHSS auction 19-20 September 2026 · Scott 117 · G grill · red Paid

@region title
# Scott 117 — 1869 12¢ green S.S. Adriatic, G grill

National Bank Note pictorial of the Collins Line steamship *Adriatic* — built to take the New York–Liverpool mail contract from Cunard, fast and ruinously expensive to run. Solo use was the 12¢ half-ounce rate to England (January 1868 to January 1870). The red strike on this example is a Paid cancel, the exchange-office mark that the letter went fully prepaid. Scott U.S. Specialized 2023 used $130. Notes after [The Swedish Tiger](https://www.theswedishtiger.com/117-scotts.html).

@narrative
  - en-US: |
      Scott one seventeen.
      [pause]
      Twelve-cent green. The steamship Adriatic. Eighteen sixty-nine pictorials again — and this time the vignette is a ship built to carry the mail.
      [pause]
      The Collins Line wanted Cunard’s New York to Liverpool contract. They built the fastest wooden steamers on the Atlantic — running water, a hairdressing salon, eighty-seven tons of coal a day. Congress subsidized them. Two ships were lost. The Adriatic was the replacement. That is the vessel on this stamp.
  - en-US: |
      Twelve cents, January eighteen sixty-eight to January eighteen seventy, was the half-ounce letter to England. Same treaty rate as Scott ninety, now on a picture of the ship that raced for that route.
      [pause]
      The red on the face is a Paid cancel — the exchange office marking that postage was fully prepaid, not a town datestamp. Red Paid All is how New York sent a letter into the British system. That is the interesting strike here.
  - en-US: |
      G grill on the reverse. Some foxing on the back, as the card hints. Scott United States Specialized, twenty twenty-three: used, one hundred thirty dollars.
      [pause]
      Then bid — this is Scott one seventeen.

