@region header
GHSS auction 19-20 September 2026 · Scott 119 · G grill · shifted frame

@region title
# Scott 119 — 1869 15¢ brown & blue Landing of Columbus, Type II

National Bank Note · first U.S. bicolor postage: blue vignette and brown frame printed in two passes. This example shows a strongly shifted frame — the landing scene sits off-register in the oval, the usual consequence of that two-color process. Type II has a complete picture frame around the vignette (Type I, Scott 118, breaks at top). Fifteen cents paid the French treaty rate and the domestic registry fee. Scott U.S. Specialized 2023 used $190. Notes after [The Swedish Tiger](https://www.theswedishtiger.com/119-scotts.html).

@narrative
  - en-US: |
      Scott one nineteen.
      [pause]
      Fifteen-cent brown and blue. Landing of Columbus. Type Two.
      [pause]
      Eighteen sixty-nine again — and here National Bank Note tried two colors on one stamp. Blue for the landing party, brown for the frame, two trips through the press. When the sheet did not land on the same pins, the picture shifted inside the oval. That is not damage. That is the bicolor process, and this example shows it strongly.
  - en-US: |
      Look at the detailed view. The vignette is off to one side of the brown frame. Type Two is the complete frameline around that picture — Type One, Scott one eighteen, breaks at the top and is much scarcer.
      [pause]
      Fifteen cents paid the eighteen fifty-seven treaty rate to France — a quarter-ounce by American packet or via England. It also paid the domestic registry fee, and it made up fifteen-cent rates across Europe.
  - en-US: |
      G grill on the reverse. Scott United States Specialized, twenty twenty-three: used, one hundred ninety dollars.
      [pause]
      Confirm Type Two. Enjoy the shifted frame. Then bid — this is Scott one nineteen.

