@region title
# Scott 190 — 1879 30¢ full black Hamilton

American Bank Note Company · the 1870 Hamilton die on the soft, porous paper of 1879 (Scott 165 is the earlier hard-paper printing). Thirty cents was a Bank Note high value: registered and heavy letters, and foreign postage when the 5¢ UPU rate was not enough. Alexander Hamilton — first Secretary of the Treasury — in profile. Lot card: used, $90. Notes after [The Swedish Tiger](https://www.theswedishtiger.com/190-scotts.html).

@narrative
  - en-US: |
      Scott one ninety.
      [pause]
      Thirty-cent full black. Hamilton. American Bank Note, eighteen seventy-nine.
      [pause]
      Same portrait as the eighteen-seventy National printing, now on the softer paper of the American Bank Note years. This is not a commemorative. It is a working high value — the stamp you reached for when five cents to the Universal Postal Union would not carry the letter.
  - en-US: |
      Look at Hamilton in the oval. That is the first Secretary of the Treasury, engraved for postage, not for a medal.
      [pause]
      Thirty cents paid registered foreign mail, triple-weight letters, and the leftover cents on a heavy cover to Europe or the Pacific. Off cover it still reads as the Bank Note era’s high-value workhorse.
  - en-US: |
      Used, as the card says. Scott catalog on the lot, ninety dollars.
      [pause]
      Then bid — this is Scott one ninety.

