@region title
# Scott 239 — 1893 30¢ Columbian, Columbus at La Rábida

American Bank Note · the monastery of La Rábida, where Columbus waited on the Franciscans before Isabella backed the voyage. Thirty cents was a high value of the Columbian set — parcels, heavy foreign letters, and registered combinations well above the 5¢ UPU rate. Lot card: mint hinged, thin, $225. Notes after [The Swedish Tiger](https://www.theswedishtiger.com/239-scotts.html).

