  - en-US: |
      Scott two thirty-nine.
      [pause]
      Thirty-cent Columbian. Columbus at La Rábida.
      [pause]
      The Franciscan monastery near Palos. Columbus waited there while the court decided whether to fund the voyage. The Columbian set put that cloister on a postage stamp for the Chicago fair.
  - en-US: |
      Thirty cents was not a letter rate. It was a high value — a heavy foreign letter, a parcel, a stack of registered combinations. The five-cent UPU stamp did the ordinary Atlantic work; this one did the expensive remainder.
      [pause]
      Look at the courtyard in the detailed view. That is the story of the wait before eighteen ninety-two’s four-hundredth anniversary.
  - en-US: |
      Mint, hinged, with thinning as the card notes. Catalog two hundred twenty-five dollars.
      [pause]
      Then bid — this is Scott two thirty-nine.

