@region title
# Scott 240 — 1893 50¢ Columbian, Recall of Columbus

American Bank Note · Isabella’s messenger overtaking Columbus on the road from Granada, recalling him to receive the commission for the first voyage. Fifty cents is the top working high value most collectors meet in the Columbian set before the dollar denominations. Lot card: mint hinged, thin, $450. Notes after [The Swedish Tiger](https://www.theswedishtiger.com/240-scotts.html).

@narrative
  - en-US: |
      Scott two forty.
      [pause]
      Fifty-cent Columbian. Recall of Columbus.
      [pause]
      The story is the road from Granada. Columbus had left the court. Isabella sent a courier. He turned back, and the voyage was on. The Bureau — American Bank Note — put that recall on the fifty-cent stamp of the Chicago fair.
  - en-US: |
      Fifty cents was packet and parcel money. Not the five-cent UPU letter. Not even the thirty-cent remainder. This is the stamp that closed a heavy registered foreign letter, or sat in a stock book as the last Columbian before the dollars.
      [pause]
      Look at the riders in the detailed view. That is the moment the expedition was saved.
  - en-US: |
      Mint, hinged, thinning as marked. Catalog four hundred fifty dollars.
      [pause]
      Then bid — this is Scott two forty.

